{"full":"hf:lvwerra/starmap","spaceId":"lvwerra/starmap","name":"Starmap","source":"huggingface","description":"A quiet observing desk for the night sky","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":5,"created":"2026-09-05T20:22:13.000Z","updated":"2026-09-08T10:19:32.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://lvwerra-starmap.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/lvwerra/starmap","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:42.244Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:42.244Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:42.244Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🔭","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive sky map and telescope-controller prototype for an Orion Optics OMC-140 on a Vixen GP mount. Inspired by the monochrome instrument layout of Departure Mono.","No telescope hardware is connected or controlled. The large dashed reticle locates the telescope; the small solid outline is the angular field. The eyepiece preset assumes 25 mm focal length and 50° apparent field on a 2000 mm telescope. The camera preset approximates an 11.2 × 6.3 mm sensor at 2000 mm. Optical distortion and camera rotation are not modelled."],"features":["Real observing time and location, browser geolocation, manual coordinates, location presets, Swiss address search with ground elevation, and local-time travel and playback.","28,352 HYG stars plus a bundled Gaia DR3 whole-sky layer of 140,763 sources at 7.5 < G ≤ 9. Deeper Gaia fields load on demand. Planets, Moon, Sun, all 110 Messier objects, constellations, and timestamped satellite…","Sun and Moon are filled disks at their apparent angular diameter, calculated from topocentric distance. Their size follows zoom and the chart projection; sidebar sizes are in arcminutes. Other planet markers remain…","Observer view is an upright, curved triangular sector spanning heading ±45° and altitude 0–90°. Its stereographic projection preserves circles and local angles, so the Sun and Moon stay round; angular scale varies…","Observer view includes an optional mountain skyline: 0.25° samples out to 200 km, from Mapzen Terrain Tiles, including Earth curvature. Buildings, trees and refraction are omitted. Nearby and distant terrain use…"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/lvwerra/starmap/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"7815a6d29a12c3ca940bc01f9b747e0a5b94b255e28f13e91adf5bca1ba19227","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:42.304Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:42.304Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"An interactive sky map and telescope-controller prototype for an Orion Optics OMC-140 on a Vixen GP mount. Inspired by the monochrome instrument layout of Departure Mono.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/lvwerra/starmap/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"7815a6d29a12c3ca940bc01f9b747e0a5b94b255e28f13e91adf5bca1ba19227","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/lvwerra/starmap/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:42.304Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-08T10:19:32.000Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/lvwerra/starmap/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:42.304Z","hash":"7815a6d29a12c3ca940bc01f9b747e0a5b94b255e28f13e91adf5bca1ba19227","originalBytes":16740,"storedBytes":16740,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["gaia","catalogue","satellite","stars","terrain","data","observing","star","zoom","positions","sky","coordinates","horizon","remain","time","browser","elevation","hyg","per","requests","run","server","telescope","their","cached","chart","cone","current","field","ground","including","map","npm","observer","through","view","when","above","angular","camera","each","earth","every","fields","follows","height","markers","only","public","python","retain","selected","selection","starlink","sun","two","after","available","c